diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 4479b53..bd6b5d8 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -9,6 +9,72 @@ pnpm install && pnpm run start
 
 The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 
+## Passkey UI integration
+
+Sign-in and sign-up use the existing external Times authentication service.
+Authenticated visitors see account settings inside those same pages. The service
+is outside this repository: it must implement the following contract before
+passkeys work end to end. Password sign-in remains available. No local auth server
+or credential store is introduced.
+
+Paths are relative to `https://us-central1-web-devrel-apps.cloudfunctions.net/times_cdn/api`.
+Requests and responses use JSON, credentialed CORS and secure HttpOnly sessions.
+The service must allow only configured application origins and enforce Origin/CSRF
+checks on mutations. Cross-site cookie restrictions may require deploying that
+service on the application site. No tokens are stored in localStorage.
+
+| Method/path | Request | Successful response |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| GET `session` | — | `{ user: { id, username, displayName, rpId } }` |
+| POST `passkeys/registration/options` | `{ username?, purpose: "signup" or "add", conditional, promotion }` | `{ ceremonyId, options }` |
+| POST `passkeys/registration/verify` | `{ ceremonyId, credential }` | Session |
+| POST `passkeys/authentication/options` | `{ purpose: "signin" or "reauthentication" }` | `{ ceremonyId, options }` |
+| POST `passkeys/authentication/verify` | `{ ceremonyId, credential, purpose }` | Session |
+| POST `passkeys/reauthentication/password` | `{ password }` | `{}` |
+| GET `passkeys` | — | `{ passkeys: [{ id, name, createdAt, lastUsedAt?, provider? }] }` |
+| PATCH `passkeys/:id` | `{ name }` | `{}` |
+| DELETE `passkeys/:id` | — | `{}` |
+| PATCH `account` | `{ username, displayName }` | Session |
+
+IDs and user handles are base64url; dates are ISO timestamps. Options use WebAuthn
+JSON and credentials use native `toJSON()`. `webauthn-polyfills` supplies JSON and
+capability compatibility without replacing native browser ceremonies.
+
+Backend requirements:
+
+- Use a vetted library such as `@simplewebauthn/server` for options and verification.
+  Persist public keys, counters, transports, backup/device flags and AAGUID metadata.
+  Provider information is a display hint only.
+- Generate fresh, expiring, single-use challenges bound to the session, user,
+  ceremony purpose, expected origin, configured RP ID and verification policy.
+  Reject replay, bad signatures, incorrect origins and account mismatches. Do not
+  trust client purpose flags at verification time.
+- Reserve a unique username during signup and create its account only after
+  verification. Include existing credentials in registration exclusions. Request
+  discoverable credentials. Only conditional creation after a full password login
+  may relax user presence verification; persist that decision with the challenge.
+  Explicit creation requires user presence.
+- Sign-in uses discoverable credentials. Reauthentication must use a nonempty
+  allowlist belonging exclusively to the active user, require user verification,
+  and reject assertions belonging to another account.
+- Enforce recent server-verified reauthentication and credential ownership for
+  additions, renames, removal and account changes, including direct API requests.
+  Reject removal of the last usable sign-in method.
+- Return HTTP 404 with `{ code: "UNKNOWN_CREDENTIAL" }` only for an unknown
+  authentication credential. Return `{ code: "REGISTRATION_REJECTED" }` only when
+  the service definitively did not retain a new credential. These explicit
+  responses drive optional password-manager cleanup; network failures do not.
+- List all credentials for the authenticated user. Only complete, successful
+  snapshots drive credential synchronization. Account renames signal new user
+  details; passkey nicknames only update the service record.
+
+Integration checks against a deployed service over HTTPS or localhost: register a
+passkey account, sign in via button and autofill, add a first passkey after password
+verification, cancel prompts, rename/remove keys, rename the account and reverify
+identity. Exercise unsupported browsers, service failures, duplicate registration,
+expired/replayed challenges, final-key removal and another user's credential during
+reauthentication. No application server was started for build verification.
+
 ## Tech Stack
 
 - **[Astro](https://astro.build/)**: The web framework for building content-driven websites.
